From: Dominikos Pritis <idominikos@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 03:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Ignore broken Audient iD24 mixer controls

Commit c53f5bfc3700 ("ALSA: usb-audio: Add mixer map quirk for Audient
iD24") renamed feature unit 12 so that userspace no longer adopts it as
the master playback volume.  Two more units on the device produce
controls that do not work.

MIXER_UNIT 60's descriptor is malformed: bmMixerControls is all-ones with
11 bytes of trailing junk and iMixer is 255 (lsusb prints "Junk at end of
descriptor").  The generic parser turns that into a fully programmable
16x6 matrix and creates sixteen 6-channel "ADAT-8 Volume" controls, named
after a channel-name string.  The device ACKs SET_CUR on them with the
UAC2 (ICN << 8 | OCN) addressing, but nothing documents what the cells
mean, and alsactl restore rewrites all 96 of them to -127 dB on every
boot and hot-plug.  Ignore the unit.

FEATURE_UNIT 11 stalls GET_RANGE for its Input Gain control (control 11),
so the driver falls back to a 0..1 placeholder range and logs
"11:0: cannot get min/max values for control 11 (id 11)" on every plug
and on every read of the control.  Ignore that control; the Phase
Inverter control on the same unit works and stays.

The same two entries were tested on an iD24 (bcdDevice 1.12) on 7.3-rc1
together with the unit 12 rename: the ADAT-8 controls and the Input Gain
placeholder are gone, alsactl store succeeds, and the min/max message no
longer appears.
---
diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
--- a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
@@ -525,9 +525,19 @@
  * output stays at 0 dB while the right one is attenuated, producing a
  * stereo imbalance.  Rename it so that it is not picked up as the
  * stream's master volume control.
+ *
+ * Mixer unit 60 has a malformed descriptor (bmMixerControls is all-ones
+ * with 11 bytes of trailing junk and iMixer is 255), so the generic parser
+ * turns it into a 16x6 matrix of "ADAT-8 Volume" controls named after a
+ * channel string; alsactl restore rewrites all 96 cells to -127 dB at every
+ * boot and hot-plug.  Feature unit 11 stalls GET_RANGE for Input Gain,
+ * which leaves a 0..1 placeholder range and logs "cannot get min/max
+ * values" on every read.  Drop both.
  */
 static const struct usbmix_name_map audient_id24_map[] = {
+	{ 11, NULL, 11 },		/* FU, Input Gain: GET_RANGE stalls */
 	{ 12, "Monitor Mix Playback" },	/* FU, partial channel coverage */
+	{ 60, NULL },			/* MU, malformed descriptor */
 	{}
 };
 
